<HelpTab>
    <FluentText>
        <strong>Import runs</strong> lists the recent imports for this location, newest first: when each ran, whether
        it was the scheduled run or a <strong>Run now</strong>, how it ended, and how many bookings it brought in.
    </FluentText>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Success</strong> - the import ran and bookings were created or updated. <strong>No changes</strong>
            means it ran fine but nothing had changed since last time.</li>
        <li><strong>Partial</strong> - it ran but some bookings couldn't be read; the rest still came in.</li>
        <li><strong>Login failed</strong> - the saved email or password was rejected. <strong>Failed</strong> - the
            site couldn't be reached or returned something unexpected.</li>
        <li><strong>Skipped</strong> - import is switched off for the location, or has no credentials.</li>
    </ul>
    <HelpNote>
        When a run fails, Lanyard raises an alert on <a href="/manage/alerts">Operations Alerts</a> and notifies
        Admins and the location's Managers - once, not every few minutes - and clears it automatically the next time
        an import runs cleanly.
    </HelpNote>
    <FluentText>
        Imported bookings carry a <strong>Provisional</strong> marker while they're still a hold in Just Step, so you
        can tell them apart from confirmed ones in Parties.
    </FluentText>
</HelpTab>
